PROVISIONAL V2 — TEMP ONLY — 2026-08-27 — published before source edits
Ownership: this leaf owns only new owned-output-direction-prototype evidence
and /tmp/safe-bash-owned-output-direction-prototype-* paths. No delegation.

Retain v1 createOutputOperation(context, destination), signal/output,
registerCleanup/acquire/close. Add explicit parent.child(destination) returning
an OutputOperation registered with its parent before child admission. Child
close never closes parent/siblings. Parent normal close closes descendants and
admission without fabricating EPIPE; parent abort propagates the identical first
reason transitively, then drains registered cooperative descendant cleanup.
No inference from opaque destination wrappers; callers explicitly choose child.
Reuse existing invocation registerCleanup hook; no parallel invocation lifecycle.
Late child creation/cleanup/acquisition is refused. Already admitted opaque
acquisition is not awaited: eventual resources are released, rejection observed.
Only cooperative registered releases can be claimed drained. Normal close does
not cancel opaque work. close is idempotent and shares completion.

Curl borrowed stdin preparation: sequence upload/data/writeout reads BEFORE
stdout-owned transfer enrollment, using caller/transfer-timeout signal and a borrowed iterator
view whose return does not return/cancel the owner's iterator. Do not race an
opaque pending borrowed next against output closure. No read lease exists in v1;
therefore completion may be delayed indefinitely until the owner resolves it.
Consumed bytes belong to this curl operation; remaining bytes stay with owner
and siblings, with no rollback or universal nonhanging guarantee. Caller abort
retains existing caller precedence, not a promise to stop opaque host work.
Implementation tradeoff (source-inspected before edits): body parts with stdin
are prepared into an owned byte buffer bounded by existing maxUploadBytes before
transfer enrollment; writeout @- keeps existing maxBufferBytes. This delays the
request and replaces streaming stdin uploads with bounded prebuffering in this
temporary profile. File-only bodies remain streaming. No new core shared-input
lease or rollback is invented. Output closure alone cannot end preparation;
the caller/timeout may still terminate its own view under existing semantics.
File-backed preparation and independent curl -o/-D tasks keep their existing
transfer/invocation lifetime; stdout closure cannot terminate necessary files,
headers or independent stderr. No stage autowrap/autocancel/demand-before-start.

First operation abort reason wins, already-aborted caller wins enrollment;
public caller abort still wins existing exec outcome. Genuine command errors
are not relabeled EPIPE; existing pipefail/rightmost status remains. Cleanup
errors surface under existing invocation rules; close is not an arbitrary
try/finally exception-precedence combinator. Parent normal close vs output
abort is explicitly distinct. API details may narrow after source inspection;
any change is recorded before author cohort execution.

At most eight new logical author cases; freeze inputs before first execution.
Old original5/adapted5/57+9/author12 remain byte-identical. Separate original
baseline0/5 and r1unchanged1/5 from adapted5/5. No independent bodies inspected.
